  {
   "id": "b7e7e8ef96",
   "es": "El present perfect continuous (have/has been + -ing) cuenta una actividad que empezó antes y sigue ahora, o que hiciste mucho últimamente: I have been studying a lot lately. Con I, you, we y they: have been (I've been); con he, she e it: has been.",
